  "body": "```html\r\n<table>\r\n <tr>\r\n  <th rowspan=\"2\">Singular\r\n  <td colspan=\"2\">it\r\n\r\n <tr>\r\n  <td rowspan=\"2\">they\r\n  <td rowspan=\"2\">them\r\n\r\n <tr>\r\n  <th>Plural\r\n</table>\r\n```\r\nRenders as two rows rather than three. As far as I can tell from https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#table-processing-model three rows is correct (conformance checker seemingly agrees with this).\r\n\r\nHowever, https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#tables-2 is super vague about rendering rowspan:\r\n\r\n> For the purposes of the CSS table model, the colspan and rowspan attributes on td and th elements are expected to provide the special knowledge regarding cells spanning rows and columns.\r\n\r\n@dbaron @tabatkins thoughts?",
